{"aaData": [["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-appear-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/appear\" title=\"APPEAR [appear]\">APPEAR [appear]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-ask-for-1\" title=\"ǃʼhoeʼa\">ǃʼhoeʼa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/ask-for\" title=\"ASK FOR [ask-for]\">ASK FOR [ask-for]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5749008211\" title=\"1 V 2 ng+3\">1 V 2 ng+3</a>", "alternative form ǃʼhoeʼin"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-be-a-hunter-1\" title=\"ng X\">ng X</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-a-hunter\" title=\"BE A HUNTER [be-a-hunter]\">BE A HUNTER [be-a-hunter]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "The copula ng is used to express &#x27;X is Y&#x27;, with Y being a noun; there is no data what the word for &#x27;hunter&#x27; is; if there is a noun &#x27;hunter&#x27;, then the construction &#x27;X ng Y&#x27; will be used, but it is possible that one can only say &#x27;X hunts&#x27;; needs to be checked with speakers."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-be-dry-1\" title=\"ǁoo\">ǁoo</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-dry\" title=\"BE DRY [be-dry]\">BE DRY [be-dry]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "ǁoo is &#x27;to dry (intr.), &#x27;to become dry&#x27;; &#x27;to be dry&#x27; is normally formed with the stative suffix -a, but there are also examples where ǁoo alone means &#x27;be dry&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-be-hungry-1\" title=\"khinn ǁqann\">khinn ǁqann</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-hungry\" title=\"BE HUNGRY [be-hungry]\">BE HUNGRY [be-hungry]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "lexicalized expression; literally &#x27;feel hunger&#x27;; ǁqann is a noun meaning &#x27;hunger&#x27;, but it is also a verb meaning &#x27;to stab&#x27;; N.B.: &#x27;to be thirsty&#x27; is literally &#x27;to feel the sun&#x27;"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-be-ill-1\" title=\"ʘʼuiʼi\">ʘʼuiʼi</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-ill\" title=\"BE ILL [be-ill]\">BE ILL [be-ill]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "means &#x27;be sick&#x27;, &#x27;be ill&#x27;, or &#x27;be sore&#x27;; an alternative way to express &#x27;to have pain&#x27; is with the verb &#x27;bite&#x27;, e.g. &#x27;my arm bites&#x27;"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-be-sad-1\" title=\"idiomatic expressions\">idiomatic expressions</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-sad\" title=\"BE SAD [be-sad]\">BE SAD [be-sad]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "various idiomatic expressions: &#x27;the heart is sore&#x27;; &#x27;the heart is not well&#x27;, etc."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-beat-2\" title=\"ǂamʼa\">ǂamʼa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/beat\" title=\"BEAT [beat]\">BEAT [beat]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "alternative forms: ǂamʼin and ǂam"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-beat-1\" title=\"ǀkxʼaike\">ǀkxʼaike</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/beat\" title=\"BEAT [beat]\">BEAT [beat]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-blink-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/blink\" title=\"BLINK [blink]\">BLINK [blink]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-boil-1\" title=\"ǀuun\">ǀuun</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/boil\" title=\"BOIL [boil]\">BOIL [boil]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-break-1\" title=\"ǁhaa\">ǁhaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/break\" title=\"BREAK [break]\">BREAK [break]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "There might be an alternation with &#x27;A V P&#x27; meaning &#x27;break off a piece of s.th.&#x27;, but it should be checked."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-bring-1\" title=\"tsaa\">tsaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/bring\" title=\"BRING [bring]\">BRING [bring]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748949939\" title=\"1 V 2-dat 3\">1 V 2-dat 3</a>", "Eastern dialect; might be the same as &#x27;bring&#x27;, which is often tsaa-a, but sometimes also just tsaa."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-build-1\" title=\"kxʼuu\">kxʼuu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/build\" title=\"BUILD [build]\">BUILD [build]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "The verb means basically &#x27;do&#x27; and &#x27;make&#x27;; it also is used in all translational equivalents of &#x27;build&#x27;; furthermore, it is used as a causative marker (cf. the causative alternation)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-burn-tr-1\" title=\"ǂʼhubi\">ǂʼhubi</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/burn-tr\" title=\"BURN (tr) [burn-tr]\">BURN (tr) [burn-tr]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-carry-1\" title=\"ǃxau\">ǃxau</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/carry\" title=\"CARRY [carry]\">CARRY [carry]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "means to carry s.th. in one&#x27;s arms or on one&#x27;s back; appears sometimes with unclear -a suffix"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-climb-1\" title=\"ǁain\">ǁain</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/climb\" title=\"CLIMB [climb]\">CLIMB [climb]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "The meaning of ǁain is rather &#x27;go up, ascend&#x27;, with manner (&#x27;climbing&#x27;) not explicitly specified."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-cook-1\" title=\"ǃxama\">ǃxama</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cook\" title=\"COOK [cook]\">COOK [cook]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "NB: For intr. &#x27;cook&#x27; (&#x27;he cooks&#x27;), &#x27;kxǁuu aa(ki)&#x27;, lit.: &#x27;make food&#x27; is frequently used."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-cough-1\" title=\"ǁʼhoqo\">ǁʼhoqo</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cough\" title=\"COUGH [cough]\">COUGH [cough]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "Some alternations might be possible with this verb (cf. comments in alternation list), but there are no examples in the corpus."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-cover-1\" title=\"ǂanu\">ǂanu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cover\" title=\"COVER [cover]\">COVER [cover]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "speaker B only; means also &#x27;close, shut&#x27; (cf. Afrikaans &#x27;toemaak&#x27;); other verbs used by the different speakers are ǂʼanʼam (C, E) and ǂʼaoke (F)"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-cover-2\" title=\"ǂʼaoke\">ǂʼaoke</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cover\" title=\"COVER [cover]\">COVER [cover]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "means basically &#x27;close, shut&#x27;, but is also used for &#x27;cover&#x27; (just like Afrikaans &#x27;toemaak&#x27;); used by speaker F only; other verbs used by the different speakers are ǂʼanʼam (C, E) and ǂanu (B)"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-cry-1\" title=\"kxʼaa\">kxʼaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cry\" title=\"CRY [cry]\">CRY [cry]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "means also &#x27;scream&#x27;; kxʼaa nǀa X &#x27;cry/shout with X&#x27; was once spontaneously used for &#x27;scold X&#x27;, which we do not include under this meaning label"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-cut-1\" title=\"ǀaa\">ǀaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cut\" title=\"CUT [cut]\">CUT [cut]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "alternative form: ǀai"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-die-1\" title=\"ǀʼaa\">ǀʼaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/die\" title=\"DIE [die]\">DIE [die]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-dig-1\" title=\"ǁʼau\">ǁʼau</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/dig\" title=\"DIG [dig]\">DIG [dig]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-dress-2\" title=\"nǁaa\">nǁaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/dress\" title=\"DRESS [dress]\">DRESS [dress]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "The P in the basic coding frame can be either the person that gets dressed (cf. ex. 38) or the thing put on (cf. ex. 35)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-dress-1\" title=\"ǂaasinn\">ǂaasinn</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/dress\" title=\"DRESS [dress]\">DRESS [dress]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "The P in the basic coding frame can be either the person that gets dressed (&#x27;She dresses me&#x27;, cf. ex. 36) or the thing put on (&#x27;I put my clothes on&#x27;, cf. ex. 264)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-eat-1\" title=\"ain\">ain</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/eat\" title=\"EAT [eat]\">EAT [eat]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "alternating form: aan"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-fall-1\" title=\"ǂqau kiin\">ǂqau kiin</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/fall\" title=\"FALL [fall]\">FALL [fall]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-fear-1\" title=\"ǃauka\">ǃauka</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/fear\" title=\"FEAR [fear]\">FEAR [fear]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748964459\" title=\"1 V ng+2\">1 V ng+2</a>", "ǃauke literally means &#x27;tremble, shiver&#x27;, but it can also mean &#x27;become afraid&#x27;; used with the STAT suffix -a (ǃau-ke-a &gt; ǃauka&#x27; (&#x27;become.afraid-STAT&#x27;)) it means &#x27;fear, be afraid&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-feel-cold-1\" title=\"ǀʼhuu\">ǀʼhuu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/feel-cold\" title=\"FEEL COLD [feel-cold]\">FEEL COLD [feel-cold]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "For some of the speakers ǀʼhuu is a noun meaning &#x27;cold wind&#x27; or &#x27;cold weather&#x27;; for other speakers, the expression khinn ǀʼhuu is lexicalized and they don&#x27;t regard ǀʼhuu as an independent noun anymore; at least two speakers (both Eastern dialect) treat ǀʼhuu alone as a verb meaning &#x27;feel cold&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-feel-cold-2\" title=\"khinn ǀʼhuu\">khinn ǀʼhuu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/feel-cold\" title=\"FEEL COLD [feel-cold]\">FEEL COLD [feel-cold]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "lit.: khinn ǀʼhuu = &#x27;feel cold(ness)&#x27;; its difficult to say if the coding frame is A V P, but at least for some of the speakers ǀʼhuu is a noun meaning &#x27;cold wind&#x27; or &#x27;cold weather&#x27;; for other speakers, the expression khinn ǀʼhuu is lexicalized and they don&#x27;t regard ǀʼhuu as an independent noun anymore; at least two speakers (both Eastern dialect) treat ǀʼhuu alone as a verb meaning &#x27;feel cold&#x27;, so the coding frame would be S V for these speakers"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-feel-pain-1\" title=\"ʘʼuiʼi\">ʘʼuiʼi</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/feel-pain\" title=\"FEEL PAIN [feel-pain]\">FEEL PAIN [feel-pain]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "means &#x27;be sick&#x27;, &#x27;be ill&#x27;, or &#x27;be sore&#x27;; an alternative way to express &#x27;to have pain&#x27; is with the verb &#x27;bite&#x27;, e.g. &#x27;my arm bites&#x27;"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-fill-1\" title=\"ǂunn\">ǂunn</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/fill\" title=\"FILL [fill]\">FILL [fill]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "lots of variation; for some speakers, ǂunn basically means &#x27;fill&#x27;, for others it basically means &#x27;be full&#x27;. Accordingly, the verb can be used with or without the causative marker (ǀkxʼui CAUS in Eastern, kxʼuu &#x27;do, make&#x27; in Western dialect), without change in meaning (see alternations below)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-follow-1\" title=\"ǀhunn\">ǀhunn</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/follow\" title=\"FOLLOW [follow]\">FOLLOW [follow]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-frighten-1\" title=\"kxʼuu qain\">kxʼuu qain</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/frighten\" title=\"FRIGHTEN [frighten]\">FRIGHTEN [frighten]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "This is a causative formation: kxʼuu/ǀkxʼui &#x27; CAUS (Western/Eastern dialect)&#x27; + qain &#x27;be.frightened&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-get-1\" title=\"hoo\">hoo</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/get\" title=\"GET [get]\">GET [get]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "A and B also have an alternative form mhoo or moo, and maa; it basically means &#x27;get&#x27;, but it can also mean &#x27;find&#x27; and &#x27;meet&#x27; (just like Afrikaans &#x27;kry&#x27;)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-give-2\" title=\"tsaa\">tsaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/give\" title=\"GIVE [give]\">GIVE [give]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748949939\" title=\"1 V 2-dat 3\">1 V 2-dat 3</a>", "Eastern dialect; might be the same as &#x27;bring&#x27;, which is often tsaa-a, but sometimes also just tsaa."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-give-1\" title=\"aa\">aa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/give\" title=\"GIVE [give]\">GIVE [give]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748949939\" title=\"1 V 2-dat 3\">1 V 2-dat 3</a>", "Western dialect, but occasionally used by Eastern dialect speakers, too."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-go-1\" title=\"ǁʼaa\">ǁʼaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/go\" title=\"GO [go]\">GO [go]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "An alternative form is ǁʼae. The verb means &#x27;go away&#x27; when used intransitively, but &#x27;go (away) to&#x27; when used transitively."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-grind-1\" title=\"ǂxaike\">ǂxaike</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/grind\" title=\"GRIND [grind]\">GRIND [grind]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-hear-1\" title=\"tyuu\">tyuu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hear\" title=\"HEAR [hear]\">HEAR [hear]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "also used for &#x27;understand&#x27;"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-help-1\" title=\"hui\">hui</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/help\" title=\"HELP [help]\">HELP [help]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-hide-1\" title=\"ǀʼhoo ǁhoo\">ǀʼhoo ǁhoo</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hide\" title=\"HIDE [hide]\">HIDE [hide]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "There are many different verbs (or verb forms?) for &#x27;hide&#x27;, we still have to check all of them (ǀoqeke, ǀʼhoo ǁhoo ǀoqe ǁhoo, ǀoqe ǀʼee, etc.), they might all be based on the same root which can be combined with different suffixes or verbs: this is only one example for the use of &#x27;hide&#x27; in the specified context (&#x27;to hide s.th.&#x27;). It is very likely that the second part is ǁhoo &#x27;put down, put aside&#x27;; in general, this verb is still very unclear and needs to be checked&lt; there is also a lot of idiolectal variation, almost every speaker seems to have a different verb or form; the &#x27;hiding affectee&#x27; cannot be specified within the coding frame of this verb (a complex sentence such as &#x27;he hides it so that she cannot see it&#x27; would be used)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-hit-1\" title=\"ǀkxʼaike\">ǀkxʼaike</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hit\" title=\"HIT [hit]\">HIT [hit]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-hit-2\" title=\"ǂamʼa\">ǂamʼa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hit\" title=\"HIT [hit]\">HIT [hit]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "alternative forms: ǂamʼin and ǂam"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-hug-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hug\" title=\"HUG [hug]\">HUG [hug]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-jump-1\" title=\"ǂkhuun\">ǂkhuun</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/jump\" title=\"JUMP [jump]\">JUMP [jump]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "In the corpus, ǂhuun alone is very rare; in most of the examples, it is followed by a path verb (or particle) (&#x27;go.away&#x27;, &#x27;go.in&#x27;, &#x27;around&#x27;, &#x27;up&#x27;, etc.)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-kill-1\" title=\"ǀhaa\">ǀhaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/kill\" title=\"KILL [kill]\">KILL [kill]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-know-1\" title=\"ǁxae\">ǁxae</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/know\" title=\"KNOW [know]\">KNOW [know]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "occurs often, but not always with a suffix -a of unclear meaning"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-laugh-1\" title=\"kxʼainʼa\">kxʼainʼa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/laugh\" title=\"LAUGH [laugh]\">LAUGH [laugh]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "An alternative form is kxʼainʼin."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-leave-1\" title=\"xuu\">xuu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/leave\" title=\"LEAVE [leave]\">LEAVE [leave]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "This verb also means &#x27;leave someone/something alone&#x27; or &#x27;stop (doing something)&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-like-1\" title=\"tsʼaanʼa\">tsʼaanʼa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/like\" title=\"LIKE [like]\">LIKE [like]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-live-2\" title=\"ǀʼhoa\">ǀʼhoa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/live\" title=\"LIVE [live]\">LIVE [live]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "means basically &#x27;to settle (somewhere)&#x27;, but can also be used for &#x27;to stay (somewhere)&#x27;"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-live-1\" title=\"nǁaa\">nǁaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/live\" title=\"LIVE [live]\">LIVE [live]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "This verbs means &#x27;be at&#x27; or &#x27;stay&#x27;, but it is also used in the sense of &#x27;He lives in/at X&#x27;; it is sometimes ka nǁaa, or nǁaa-in; an alternative candidate for this meaning is ǀʼhoa &#x27;settle&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-load-1\" title=\"nǃao\">nǃao</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/load\" title=\"LOAD [load]\">LOAD [load]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5749008211\" title=\"1 V 2 ng+3\">1 V 2 ng+3</a>", "The basic coding frame &#x27;A V P ng X&#x27; can be used for both &#x27;A loads P on X&#x27; and &#x27;A loads P with X&#x27;. When used in an &#x27;A V P&#x27; construction, all speakers allow e.g. both &#x27;He loads pears&#x27; and &#x27;He loads the cart&#x27;, but the &#x27;cart&#x27; example can alternatively have an oblique object in an &#x27;A V ng X&#x27; construction. When both &#x27;pears&#x27; and &#x27;cart&#x27; are expressed, speakers strongly prefer the &#x27;pears&#x27; to be the direct object and the &#x27;cart&#x27; to be the oblique object, but generally at least some speakers accept also the variant with the &#x27;cart&#x27; as direct object and the &#x27;pears&#x27; as oblique, or alternatively, the &#x27;pears&#x27; as a comitative/instrumental argument with nǀa."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-look-at-1\" title=\"ǂaqe\">ǂaqe</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/look-at\" title=\"LOOK AT [look-at]\">LOOK AT [look-at]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-make-1\" title=\"kxʼuu\">kxʼuu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/make\" title=\"MAKE [make]\">MAKE [make]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "The verb means basically &#x27;do&#x27; and &#x27;make&#x27;; it also is used in all translational equivalents of &#x27;build&#x27;; furthermore, it is used as a causative marker (cf. the causative alternation)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-meet-1\" title=\"hoo\">hoo</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/meet\" title=\"MEET [meet]\">MEET [meet]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "A and B also have an alternative form mhoo or moo, and maa; it basically means &#x27;get&#x27;, but can also mean &#x27;find&#x27; and &#x27;meet&#x27; (just like Afrikaans &#x27;kry&#x27;)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-name-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/name\" title=\"NAME [name]\">NAME [name]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-peel-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/peel\" title=\"PEEL [peel]\">PEEL [peel]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-play-1\" title=\"ǃqora\">ǃqora</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/play\" title=\"PLAY [play]\">PLAY [play]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "This verb is often used with preverbal ka (presumably a partly lexicalized pluractional marker), but can also be used without it (different speakers have different preferences whether they use ka or not)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-pour-1\" title=\"ǂhaun\">ǂhaun</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/pour\" title=\"POUR [pour]\">POUR [pour]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-push-1\" title=\"ǂʼhaqa\">ǂʼhaqa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/push\" title=\"PUSH [push]\">PUSH [push]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "It is difficult to give a citation form and basic coding frame for this verb; &#x27;push&#x27; is normally translated as ǂʼhaqa, but very often it appears in a SVC with a path verb ǁʼaa (alternative form ǁʼae), &#x27;(go) away&#x27;, when there is no other direction specified; ǁʼaa can be replaced by other path verbs if a different specific path (&#x27;into&#x27;, &#x27;towards&#x27;) is specified."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-put-1\" title=\"ǁhoo\">ǁhoo</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/put\" title=\"PUT [put]\">PUT [put]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5749008211\" title=\"1 V 2 ng+3\">1 V 2 ng+3</a>", "There is no general verb meaning &#x27;put&#x27;; ǁhoo means &#x27;put s.th. down&#x27; but there are a lot of other &#x27;put verbs&#x27; like ǀʼee &#x27;go in, put in&#x27;, ʘquu &#x27;put in&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-rain-1\" title=\"ǂhau\">ǂhau</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/rain\" title=\"RAIN [rain]\">RAIN [rain]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "only possible with a subject meaning &#x27;rain&#x27; (noun) (ǂhuu in Western dialect, ǃhaqa in Eastern dialect)"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-roll-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/roll\" title=\"ROLL [roll]\">ROLL [roll]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-run-1\" title=\"ǃae\">ǃae</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/run\" title=\"RUN [run]\">RUN [run]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", "sounds often like ǃaea, without any obvious reason why there should be an suffix -a"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-say-1\" title=\"ku\">ku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/say\" title=\"SAY [say]\">SAY [say]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5781075063\" title=\"1 V ng+2 UTT3\">1 V ng+2 UTT3</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-scream-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/scream\" title=\"SCREAM [scream]\">SCREAM [scream]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-search-for-2\" title=\"ǂxaqake\">ǂxaqake</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/search-for\" title=\"SEARCH FOR [search-for]\">SEARCH FOR [search-for]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "Western dialect only; this verb means basically &#x27;look for, search&#x27;; it is used frequently by speaker A only to express &#x27;want&#x27; (note that this corresponds to Afrikaans &#x27;ek soek ...&#x27; = &#x27;I want ...&#x27;)"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-search-for-1\" title=\"ǁaanʼa\">ǁaanʼa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/search-for\" title=\"SEARCH FOR [search-for]\">SEARCH FOR [search-for]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "alternative form: ǁaanʼin; Western dialect only; alternative form: ǁaaʼin"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-see-1\" title=\"nǀai\">nǀai</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/see\" title=\"SEE [see]\">SEE [see]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "alternative form nǀaa"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-send-1\" title=\"ǀae\">ǀae</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/send\" title=\"SEND [send]\">SEND [send]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748949939\" title=\"1 V 2-dat 3\">1 V 2-dat 3</a>", "The most basic meaning of this verb is probably &#x27;to send somebody to do something&#x27;, but in elicitation it could also be used for &#x27;to send s.th. for somebody&#x27; (the intended meaning here). There is a lot of variation as the examples show; the construction can, for example, depend on the animacy of the third argument (inanimate locations are expressed by a V + V(path) serial verb construction, with the location encoded as oblique object, whereas animates are more likely to be treated as beneficiaries (encoded as Dative objects, with a BEN suffix -a on the verb), etc. Furthermore, the verb appears very often but not always, with a suffix -a; in many cases this could be interpreted as the (productive) BEN suffix, but there are also cases where one would expect the BEN suffix (e.g. examples with a Dative recipient), but there is no such a suffix (ex. 22), and cases where one would not expect a BEN suffix, but where one finds a suffix -a; furthermore, the -a suffix is normally not found in IRR constructions, which would not be the case if it was a BEN suffix; the use of the suffix -a with ǀae might thus depend on speakers&#x27; choice/preference; it could also be a (not completely) lexicalized suffix; the data in the corpus (both naturally spoken and elicited), until now, do not allow to set up any specific rule for the use or non-use of this suffix."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-shave-a-body-part_person-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/shave-a-body-part_person\" title=\"SHAVE (a body part/person) [shave-a-body-part_person]\">SHAVE (a body part/person) [shave-a-body-part_person]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-shout-at-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/shout-at\" title=\"SHOUT AT [shout-at]\">SHOUT AT [shout-at]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-show-2\" title=\"qann\">qann</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/show\" title=\"SHOW [show]\">SHOW [show]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748949939\" title=\"1 V 2-dat 3\">1 V 2-dat 3</a>", "Eastern dialect (= speakers A, B, K only); the citation form is qann or qann-ya, but in the corpus this verb is always used in the form qann-ya; the element -ya is probably the benefactive suffix, which is very productive."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-show-1\" title=\"kadyama\">kadyama</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/show\" title=\"SHOW [show]\">SHOW [show]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748949939\" title=\"1 V 2-dat 3\">1 V 2-dat 3</a>", "Western dialect"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-sing-1\" title=\"ǂeeke\">ǂeeke</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/sing\" title=\"SING [sing]\">SING [sing]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655420783\" title=\"1 V\">1 V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-sink-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/sink\" title=\"SINK [sink]\">SINK [sink]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-sit-down-1\" title=\"suin , ǃʼhaun\">suin , ǃʼhaun</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/sit-down\" title=\"SIT DOWN [sit-down]\">SIT DOWN [sit-down]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "With a singular subject, it is suin in the Western dialect, and tcuin in the Eastern dialect; with plural subjects, the suppletive stem ǃʼaun is used."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-sit-1\" title=\"soo\">soo</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/sit\" title=\"SIT [sit]\">SIT [sit]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "Western dialect soo, Eastern dialect tcoo"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-smell-1\" title=\"ǃqhao\">ǃqhao</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/smell\" title=\"SMELL [smell]\">SMELL [smell]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-steal-1\" title=\"gaake\">gaake</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/steal\" title=\"STEAL [steal]\">STEAL [steal]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "Note that normally the P/X is the thing stolen, but there are also examples where it is the &#x27;stealing source&#x27; (cf. ex. 274)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-take-1\" title=\"ǀai\">ǀai</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/take\" title=\"TAKE [take]\">TAKE [take]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "This verb means &#x27;take&#x27;. It is also occasionally used for &#x27;to touch (something)&#x27;, but there is no verb that corresponds to &#x27;touch&#x27; in general."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-talk-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/talk\" title=\"TALK [talk]\">TALK [talk]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-tear-1\" title=\"tyxaa\">tyxaa</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/tear\" title=\"TEAR [tear]\">TEAR [tear]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-tell-1\" title=\"ǀkxʼae\">ǀkxʼae</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/tell\" title=\"TELL [tell]\">TELL [tell]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748949939\" title=\"1 V 2-dat 3\">1 V 2-dat 3</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-think-1\" title=\"ǂʼain\">ǂʼain</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/think\" title=\"THINK [think]\">THINK [think]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748964459\" title=\"1 V ng+2\">1 V ng+2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-throw-1\" title=\"ǂaqbeke\">ǂaqbeke</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/throw\" title=\"THROW [throw]\">THROW [throw]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5749008211\" title=\"1 V 2 ng+3\">1 V 2 ng+3</a>", "alternative forms: ǂaqbe (+ path verb), ǂaqma (+ path verb); lots of variation; the -ke is a suffix with unclear meaning that appears also with other verbs; in SVCs (with path verbs like &#x27;go.to / go.away&#x27;, &#x27;come&#x27;, &#x27;put.in&#x27;) the -ke is deleted"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-tie-1\" title=\"ǁʼngke\">ǁʼngke</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/tie\" title=\"TIE [tie]\">TIE [tie]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5749008211\" title=\"1 V 2 ng+3\">1 V 2 ng+3</a>", "Western dialect ǁʼ(a)ngke, Eastern dialect nǁngke; can mean &#x27;attach by tying&#x27;, &#x27;fasten&#x27;, or &#x27;tie up&#x27;"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-touch-1\" title=\"ǀai\">ǀai</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/touch\" title=\"TOUCH [touch]\">TOUCH [touch]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5748964459\" title=\"1 V ng+2\">1 V ng+2</a>", "This verb means &#x27;take&#x27;. It is also occasionally used for &#x27;to touch (something)&#x27;, but there is no verb that corresponds to &#x27;touch&#x27; in general."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-want-2\" title=\"ǂxaqake\">ǂxaqake</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/want\" title=\"WANT [want]\">WANT [want]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "Western dialect only; this verb means basically &#x27;look for, search&#x27;; it is used frequently by speaker A only to express &#x27;want&#x27; (note that this corresponds to Afrikaans &#x27;ek soek ...&#x27; = &#x27;I want ...&#x27;)"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-want-1\" title=\"ǂao\">ǂao</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/want\" title=\"WANT [want]\">WANT [want]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", "Some speakers prefer to use this verb with a suffix -a (with unclear meaning, maybe the partly lexicalized perfective/stative suffix) whereas other speakers normally use it without the suffix."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-wash-1\" title=\"ǁkxʼam\">ǁkxʼam</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/wash\" title=\"WASH [wash]\">WASH [wash]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5655417010\" title=\"1 V 2\">1 V 2</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nuuu1241-wipe-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/wipe\" title=\"WIPE [wipe]\">WIPE [wipe]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017620495\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "The usage of loanwords is sporadic and inconsistent."]], "sEcho": "1", "iTotalRecords": 96, "iTotalDisplayRecords": 96}